<DIV><FONT size="1" style="font-size:1pt;color:white">            Sezzle Inc. (ASX:SZL) | ARBN 633 327 358 | sezzle.com | 251 1st Ave N, Suite 200, Minneapolis, MN 55401    1  31 July 2023   ASX RELEASE  Company Announcements Platform    June Business Update  Gaining momentum with over 187,0001 subscribers across Premium and  Anywhere    Sezzle Inc. (ASX:SZL) (Sezzle or Company) // Purpose-driven digital payment platform, Sezzle, is pleased  to provide the market with an update on key financial metrics for the month ended 30 June 2023.2    &quot;I am thrilled to see the continued success of our initiatives and the promise that our new product launches are  showing,&#8221; stated Charlie Youakim, Sezzle Chairman and CEO. &#8220;The June launch of Sezzle Anywhere has been  particularly exciting, driving our total subscriber base (Premium and Anywhere) to over 187,000. Sezzle  Anywhere is making an immediate impact on our business, as we are experiencing a pickup in consumer  activity, and we are seeing that flow through preliminary July to-date results.&quot;    Financial Highlights  &#8226; Total Income grew to US$11.8 million (A$17.6 million3) in June 2023, representing a 20.7% YoY increase.  Total Income as a percentage of Underlying Merchant Sales (UMS) increased 153 bps YoY to 9.1%.   &#8226; In June, Sezzle recorded GAAP Net Income of US$1.2 million, resulting in GAAP Net Income of US$1.1  million for the quarter and representing the fourth straight quarter of GAAP Net Income for the  Company.     1 Premium and Anywhere subscribers as of 30 July 2023.  2 Results are unaudited preliminary financial results.    3 A$ to US$ exchange rate of $0.6721 as of 30 June 2023.  </FONT></DIV>
<P><HR noshade><P>
<DIV style="page-break-before:always;">&nbsp;</DIV>
</DIV>
<!-- szl-230730ex9901002.jpg -->
<DIV style="padding-top:2em;">
<IMG src="szl-230730ex9901002.jpg" title="slide2" width="1055" height="1365">
<DIV><FONT size="1" style="font-size:1pt;color:white">            Sezzle Inc. (ASX:SZL) | ARBN 633 327 358 | sezzle.com | 251 1st Ave N, Suite 200, Minneapolis, MN 55401    2  &#8226; The Company posted Adjusted EBTDA and Adjusted EBITDA (non-GAAP measures) of US$1.2 million  and US$2.5 million, respectively, for the month of June. For the quarter ended 30 June 2023, Adjusted  EBTDA and Adjusted EBITDA were US$2.5 million and US$6.4 million, respectively.   &#8226; As of 30 June 2023, Sezzle retained abundant capital and liquidity with US$63.4 million of cash on  hand (US$1.3 million restricted) and US$58.3 million drawn on its US$100 million credit facility.  &#8226; As of 30 June 2023, notes receivable (net) and merchant accounts payable amounted to US$83.8  million and US$67.4 million, respectively. The merchant interest program represented US$52.4 million  of the merchant accounts payable balance.    Other Notable Items  &#8226; Sezzle Canada recently surpassed the milestone of 500,000 users, reaching the mark in just four years.  Consumer loyalty in Canada is strong with the top 10% of Sezzle&#8217;s Canadian shoppers making an  average of 23 purchases per year. In addition, the Sezzle app consistently has the highest rating amongst  Buy Now, Pay Later apps on the Canadian App Store. These achievements are a testament to Sezzle's  commitment to superior execution and a great product offering. The Company remains dedicated to  continued investment in the region.   &#8226; Nasdaq Listing. Sezzle is waiting for final approval of the Registration Statement after filing Amendment  No. 2 to Form S-1 with the SEC on 28 July 2023. Pending any additional final deliveries with the SEC  and the Nasdaq, the Company is on track to go live on the Nasdaq Capital Market shortly thereafter.  &#8226; Second Quarter Earnings Call. The Company will host its second quarter earnings conference call on  the morning of 9 August at 10.30 am (Sydney time). To register for the call, please navigate to:  https://s1.c-conf.com/diamondpass/10032520-pugdsx.html. Upon registration, participants will receive  the dial in number.     </FONT></DIV>
